[
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Software engineering is the practice of using computers and computing to help solve problems, focusing on the computer as a problem‑solving tool rather than on hardware design or purely theoretical aspects.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "As software engineers, we use our knowledge of computers and computing to help solve problems.",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "We can view computing in a similar light. We can concentrate on the computers and programming languages, or we can view them as tools to be used in designing and implementing a solution to a problem. Software engineering takes the latter view, as shown in Figure 1.3. Instead of investigating hardware design or proving theorems about how algorithms work,a software engineer focuses on the computer as a problem solving tool.",
                "img_id": "img0_se_theory_practice.pdf__chunk_144_144_44"
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "In relation to computer science, software engineering fits by applying computing as a tool to design and implement solutions, i.e., solving problems with a structured engineering approach rather than focusing solely on theoretical computing or hardware.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "We can view computing in a similar light. We can concentrate on the computers and programming languages, or we can view them as tools to be used in designing and implementing a solution to a problem. Software engineering takes the latter view, as shown in Figure 1.3.",
                "img_id": "img0_se_theory_practice.pdf__chunk_144_144_44"
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Instead of investigating hardware design or proving theorems about how algorithms work,a software engineer focuses on the computer as a problem solving tool.",
                "img_id": "img0_se_theory_practice.pdf__chunk_144_144_44"
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    }
]

[
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "Technical quality focuses on the product and its performance, measured with metrics like faults, failures, and timing, while business quality is the quality viewed in terms of the products and services being provided by the business in which the software is embedded; thus, quality assessment should include both the technical value and the business value of the software.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "When the focus of quality assessment is on products and processes, we usually measure quality with mathematical expressions involving faults, failures, and timing.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "That is, we look at the technical value of our products, rather than more broadly at their business value, and we make decisions based only on the resulting products' technical quality.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "In other words, we measure the quality [of our software] by the obvious metrics: up versus down time, maintenance costs, costs connected with modifications, and the like. In other words, we manage development based on operational performance within cost parameters.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Thus, our success criteria must make sense not only for software projects and processes, but also for the more general business practices they support.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "If there is not clear (expected) business value (expressed quantitatively: number of claims processed, etc.) then we can't launch a systems project.",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ],
    "type": null
  }
]

