[
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Example of black-box reuse: As consumers, we can either use a product whole, without modification (called black-box reuse). We perform black-box reuse often, when we use routines from mathematical libraries or build graphical interfaces from predefined sets of components.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "As consumers, we can either use a product whole, without modification (called black-box reuse ). We perform black-box reuse often, when we use routines from mathematical libraries or build graphical interfaces from predefined sets of components.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Benefits and key considerations of black-box reuse: Reuse has great potential for increasing productivity and reducing cost. New applications are variations of existing structures, built by assembling components from a library, which supports reuse through organized assets and standardized components.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Software researchers believe that reuse has great potential for increasing productivity and reducing cost, and some efforts to apply reuse technology confirm their belief.",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "New applications  are  variations  of  the  standard  software  structures, and  they  are  built  by  assembling components from the library.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Drawbacks and concerns: Black-box reuse must be verifiable, since we need to ensure the reused module performs its required function in an acceptable way; for code, this means being sure it is failure-free, and for test sets, ensuring they thoroughly exercise the intended function. Additionally, reuse can be accompanied by social, cultural, and legal issues, and overall reuse can feel radical or threatening to developers accustomed to building software from scratch.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "An important issue in black-box reuse is our ability to verify that a reused module performs its required function in an acceptable way. If the component is code, we want to be sure it is failure-free; if it is a test set, we want to be sure it thoroughly exercises the function for which it is intended.",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "the effort to understand and modify the component must be less than the effort to write a new equivalent component",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Reuse often seems radical and threatening to developers who are accustomed to writing software from scratch. It is clear that many social, cultural, and legal issues are involved in reuse, as well as technical ones.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    }
]

